{"id": "EUVD-2026-82308", "enisaUuid": "cf8d214c-54a3-3849-a823-b09de2cab738", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni3c: master: Fix use-after-free of master->this\n\nsysfs attribute callbacks for the master controller device dereference\nmaster->this.  However, master->this is freed in\ni3c_master_detach_free_devs() before the master device itself is\nreleased.\n\nAs a result, sysfs accesses can dereference a freed master->this\npointer, leading to a use-after-free.\n\nKeep master->this alive until i3c_masterdev_release(), which is called\nafter the master device and its sysfs state are being torn down. Do not\nfree master->this as part of the normal device detach path.\n\nOn the error path in i3c_master_set_info(), reset master->this and\nbus.cur_master to NULL before freeing the allocated device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/027679d613ea73b8a00831369ec34eea804ce1bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23a1c4288a60e253a05a882bd8928ed61beb4a48", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f3145db05fede36b35f8249b8acde5bd5d54864", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50034d8d0f797c3a7a599f750a7d3e792e80dea5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/feb0ed76601f3c2f91f08688c5a7d8b9d382f720"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93200", "GHSA-353r-jvg2-63v3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "049ee997-0cb8-384b-9b7e-6df589d01ad4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <027679d613ea73b8a00831369ec34eea804ce1bd"}, {"id": "216d0b1a-b62c-317d-ba6f-0943a80971f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "28b12ff2-7dee-39b0-b0a4-b9c0655f56e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.0"}, {"id": "3a1bef4e-9a62-3480-a57e-2306abeeab85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "518e7b88-1fce-3886-878c-a388cb1b8698", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <feb0ed76601f3c2f91f08688c5a7d8b9d382f720"}, {"id": "69a59c8c-bf6b-3753-917b-9b3b0c1f47fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "7a154935-99e2-36ec-adc4-9feeea8ab07c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "849a6b19-5e64-3c0c-825c-1c9b4ddc54af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "8b15042f-6f19-329b-9184-1928353960cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <4f3145db05fede36b35f8249b8acde5bd5d54864"}, {"id": "c13fc2d9-8f7c-3e37-b69a-b4abfb79eb88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <23a1c4288a60e253a05a882bd8928ed61beb4a48"}, {"id": "c47d5f09-2f08-3bfe-b8ae-a21d3348da8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <50034d8d0f797c3a7a599f750a7d3e792e80dea5"}, {"id": "f92ac977-0dc7-3f8b-bd61-d050ce1c88f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1b6c60b8-79d1-3885-805f-3f9ff123e010", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}